  (text "Power: SW1 common (pin 3) is VLOAD. Position SAO = badge 3.3 V (pin 1), middle = OFF (pin 2, unconnected), BAT = coin cell through D6 (pin 4)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 170.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e9a83e63-bb6f-516c-99f3-2eee33dc8c6c"))
  (text "D6 is the series cell diode required by docs/standard.md section 3: the ATtiny is wired to SAO SDA/SCL, so nothing may push current into the CR2032." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 173.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ba78d84e-527c-5c80-9bc7-ef0728848f68"))
  (text "No I2C pull-ups on the add-on (the maker's R1/R2 10k were removed; the badge provides them). SAO GPIO2 is not connected (the maker's UPDI-on-GPIO2 jumper JP1 was removed)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 177.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b7771c85-f15e-53ec-a69f-62d6b38550eb"))
  (text "JP1 (the maker's JP2): pads 1-2 bridged by copper = LEDs driven by the ATtiny (PA6). Cut the bridge and solder 2-3 = LEDs driven by the badge on SAO GPIO1." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 181.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c22de111-3b4a-548a-be32-8603e2a1a4f0"))
  (text "D1..D5: SK6805-EC3210R side-firing RGB, chained D1 -> D5 in the order the maker's firmware expects. TP1 = chain out (more LEDs), TP2 = UPDI programming pad, TP3 = GND pad." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 185.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "24a186ef-bcad-53e1-a878-6d39f6781845"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
